/*
Problem: Count Good Nodes in Binary Tree (LC 1448)
Topic: Binary Tree / DFS

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

A node is called "good" if no node on
the path from the root to that node
has a value greater than it.

While traversing the tree, keep track
of the maximum value seen so far on
the current root-to-node path.

If the current node's value is greater
than or equal to this maximum, it is a
good node.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Start DFS from the root.

2. Pass the maximum value seen on the
   current path.

3. For every node:

   • If node->val >= maxValue,
     count it as a good node.

   • Update:

     maxValue = max(maxValue,
                    node->val)

4. Recursively process the left and
   right subtrees.

5. Return the total count.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

        3
       / \
      1   4
     /   / \
    3   1   5

Good nodes:

3 (root)

4

5

3 (left leaf)

Answer:

4

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

      3
     /
    3
   /
  3

Every node equals the maximum seen.

Answer:

3

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

The variable maxValue always stores
the largest value encountered on the
current root-to-node path.

A node is good exactly when its value
is not smaller than this maximum.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Each node is visited exactly once.

Space : O(h)

h = height of the tree (recursion
stack).

Worst case: O(n)

Balanced tree: O(log n)

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

DFS / Tree Traversal
*/

class Solution {
public:

    int dfs(TreeNode* root, int maxValue) {

        if (root == NULL)
            return 0;

        int count = 0;

        // Current node is good
        if (root->val >= maxValue)
            count = 1;

        // Update maximum on this path
        maxValue = max(maxValue,
                       root->val);

        count += dfs(root->left,
                     maxValue);

        count += dfs(root->right,
                     maxValue);

        return count;
    }

    int goodNodes(TreeNode* root) {

        return dfs(root, root->val);
    }
};
